    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Paralympic",
            "zh": "残奥会的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " sports, most visually impaired athletes compete alongside a guide. The most successful pairs are usually very quiet. “During the race, we try not to speak much,” said Jerusa Geber dos Santos of Brazil of her "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "partnership",
            "ref": "v-partnership"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " with her guide, Gabriel Garcia."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Geber dos Santos lost her sight in her teens. Now 42, she holds the women’s world record in the 100-metre dash for blind or nearly blind athletes. When she races with Garcia, he runs to her left. He holds a short "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tether",
            "zh": "拴绳"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in his right hand, while she holds the other end in her left. If they’ve started well, he matches her pace step by step, but with the opposite foot. “There’s a real harmony between us,” Geber dos Santos said."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Since 2012, most Paralympic guides have received medals alongside their athletes. But the teamwork often goes beyond the finish line. While training daily with Geber dos Santos, Garcia is also preparing to run on Brazil’s men’s 4×100m Olympic "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "relay team",
            "zh": "接力跑队"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". “I prefer being a guide,” he said. “I feel more pressure at the Paralympics. I have to give 200 per cent of myself to avoid mistakes and help my teammate do her best.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The partnership between American "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "para-cyclist",
            "zh": "残疾人自行车运动员"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Hannah Chadwick and her guide, Skyler Espinoza, tells a similar story. Every time Chadwick climbs on a bike behind Espinoza, she feels Espinoza reach back to hold her hand. “It’s a reminder that we’re in this together,” said Espinoza."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Chadwick and Espinoza follow the same training plan. Sometimes, when the training gets too hard, Chadwick thinks about Espinoza. “We have the same goal,” she said. “"
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "I’m not training just for myself"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". I’m training for someone else, too!”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Espinoza, meanwhile, often hears people praise her for “sacrificing” for a disabled athlete. But she’s always quick to correct that idea. To her, it’s not a “sacrifice” at all. Espinoza believes that if she hadn’t begun piloting, she would never have "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "shone",
            "ref": "v-shine"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " so much in sports. “I’m lucky that Hannah chose me to do this, just as I chose to do it with her,” she said."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
